            <fr:title text="About the manual › Principles"><fr:link href="/0002/" title="About the manual" uri="https://coln-project.github.io/0002/" display-uri="0002" type="local">About the manual</fr:link> › Principles</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>The Coln manual is an <html:em>authoratative</html:em>, <html:em>conceptual</html:em>, and <html:em>incomplete</html:em> reference document for engaged users and developers of Coln.</html:p>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors />
                <fr:uri>https://coln-project.github.io/0005/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>0005</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/0005/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Authoratative">Authoratative</fr:title>
                <fr:taxon>Principle</fr:taxon>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>When the manual makes a definitive statement about the behavior of Coln, if the code deviates from the manual then the code is considered to have a bug.</html:p>
                <html:p>There may be points in the manual where as I am writing, I decide that the current behavior of Coln is inadequate. In these places, I will write down what I intend the behavior to be, and mark the sentence with <html:sup class="smallcaps">todo</html:sup> at the end.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors />
                <fr:uri>https://coln-project.github.io/0006/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>0006</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/0006/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Conceptual">Conceptual</fr:title>
                <fr:taxon>Principle</fr:taxon>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>The purpose of the manual is to produce <html:em>understanding</html:em>. The manual is not a specification, but a motivated reader could probably fill in the full details of a specification from the understanding imparted in the manual. Most importantly, a user of Coln who has carefully read the manual should not need to guess at what any particular piece of code means; the conceptual understanding laid out in this manual should be sufficient to give an unambiguous human-comprehensible semantics.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
