              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>This manual (like Coln itself) is currently incomplete.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <html:p>The Coln manual is <html:em>not</html:em> a tutorial. The Coln manual is <html:em>not</html:em> a place for original mathematical research. The Coln manual is <html:em>not</html:em> a development log.</html:p>
            <html:p>Moreover, the Coln manual is <html:em>not</html:em> an advertisement. The intended audience of this manual is a reader with patience and a good amount of time, who is motivated for reasons found elsewhere to learn about Coln. There may be sections where we outline the <html:em>rationale</html:em> for a design decision; these should not be interpreted as claims of the superiority of this design decision, merely as a record of the thought process that went into it.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
